{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792265849,"nonce":"qBhqObZdE8ae/I4gChbF66aoexY=","title":"Python: chaos's vectors are dynamic because dunders keep Object params","message":"chaos's `GVector` fields, `Chaosgame`'s bounds and most of its locals were `Object`. Four causes, each enough on its own:\n\n1. Every operator, comparison, item and call method (`boxed_entry`) kept dynamic parameters, because the library's hooks reach them with boxes. Their bodies (`GVector(self.x * other, ...)`) then fed `Object` into `__init__` and every field.\n2. `transform_point(self, point, trafo=None)` starts with `if trafo is None: trafo = self.get_random_trafo()`. A rebound parameter was excluded from the only-passed-None fold, so the local joined None and a tuple to `Object`, and `t`, `u`, `co1`, `co2` and `l1`/`l2` followed. `linear_combination`'s `if l2 is None: l2 = 1 - l1` is the same idiom.\n3. `functools.reduce` was typed `(Object, List(Object), Object) -\u003e Object`, so `reduce(operator.add, self.num_trafos, 0)` made `num_trafos` a `List(Object)`.\n4. A field bound to `[]` in a constructor and passed to any function was \"kept\", hence `List(Object)`, where a local follows the callee's list-parameter facts.\n\nDesign:\n\n- A dunder of a class whose instances the program never holds as a dynamic value is typed by its calls in view, like any closed method. Operator sites now also record the reflected method (`2 * v`), and comparison sites record argument types.\n- Lowering notes each class an instance of which `coerce` makes dynamic, together with the classes its fields and method results expose. Boxing into closure cells, cell prologues and generator environments is exempt, since only typed code reads those back.\n- A reading that holds a class it did not expect stops lowering, and the program is read again with that class's dunders dynamic, as record demotion already does.\n- A program that reads names by text (`eval`, `exec`, `globals`, `vars`, `locals`) holds every class from the start.\n- The hooks call dunders through `lowerer.dunder`, which converts each box to the parameter's type with a check. A flow the analysis missed therefore raises TypeError rather than misreading a box.\n- Sugar rewrites:\n  - `if p is None: p = e` at the top of a function becomes `p$set = e if p is None else p`, so the existing fold applies.\n  - `reduce(f, xs, start)` calls a generated module function that folds in a loop (`acc op x` for an `operator` function).\n  - `__rmul__ = __mul__` in a class body is a copy of the method.\n- Augmented assignment types `l op= r` through the class's method, as `l op r` already did (`s += t` on Decimals was `Object`).\n- Field lists passed to functions follow `list_params`.\n\nResult: chaos is fully typed (`GVector { x: Float, y: Float, z: Num(int|float) }`, `Chaosgame` bounds `Float`). Its per-iteration time on the Mac (Cranelift tiered) is 0.031 s -\u003e 0.0066 s. Whole-process instructions at one iteration are 5.74G -\u003e 4.49G (0.783). The suite total is 1.002, and all 22 kernels check against CPython.\n\nStill read twice:\n\n- raytrace (Vector/Point, through `firstIntersection`'s None-or-tuple; a nullable tuple type is owed).\n- telco (`decimal`'s `_coerce` returns `other` under `isinstance` without narrowing the return).\n- pyflate (`d[x.bits] = [x]`, a dict of instance lists).\n\nThe second reading costs about one compile (around 20 ms).\n\nGaps:\n\n- A library route that boxes instances without a `coerce` the lowering sees, such as typed-list sorting in generated kind code, is not noted. Such a route reaches the checked conversion instead.\n- `__iadd__` is ignored (e2cf6f0).","files":null}]}